  <iati-identifier>NL-KVK-40409352-PRJ13-106-0002</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="NL-KVK-40409352" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands Red Cross</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Access to Health 2020 - access to critical infrastructure</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Access to WASH services are a priority need for Gaza. Given the dependency of WASH interventions on the functioning of the water/waste-water/energy system, NLRC wants to support ICRC&#x2019;s and PRCS&#x2019; activities to ensure well-functioning critical infrastructure. The first step to get there, is to have the correct information and the tools to work with it. That is where this project is about.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gaza, occupied Palestinian Territories.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NLRC, PRCS, 510, ICRC</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Overall objective: By 2022, data and information that are critical for the well-functioning of basic infrastructure that serves 500.000 people  in the urban areas of Gaza, is available and can be used by local authorities, PRCS, ICRC and other relevant partners in order to improve the reliability and independence of basic infrastructure. In its turn, an independent and reliable network will contribute to the improved health of the families depending on it. 
 
&#x2022; Specific objective 1: by 2022 the SDI is in place for major stakeholder to share data and insight on critical infrastructure and focal points are appointed (and trained when necessary) to handle the data in the SDI; 
&#x2022; Specific objective 2: By 2022, PRCS has the capacity to collect, analyse and use data to strengthen their health interventions in Gaza and contribute to the SD</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims at providing insights in the gaps and needs in the existing basic infrastructure network&#x2019;s capacity to reliably provide water and evacuate waste water and to provide a platform for other (Dutch) private sector, (i)NGOs and other partners to support local solutions in bridging the gaps.  
 
With these insights a road map can be drawn towards an energy provision for Gaza that is independent from fossil fuels and more decentralized. This will make infrastructure that is critical for all sorts of WASH and health-related issues (e.g. emergency, epidemics, access to clean water and sanitation) more self-reliant and less vulnerable to stress on the network. 
 
This project provides the opportunity to add value to the existing and future emergency operations in chronic crisis settings by bringing in a unique combination of WASH and data expertise to support the activities of the Red Cross Red Crescent movement actors in the region.</narrative>
  </description>
